## Why This Is Asked
The candidate demonstrates practical understanding of idempotence in multi-tenant CNFs via sidecar patterns and Redis TTLs.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotence and deduplication per tenant
- Redis SETNX with TTL for race-free dedupe
- Sidecar data flow and fallback handling

## Code Example
```go
// simplified sketch
package main
import "net/http"
func Handle(req *http.Request) {
  tenant := req.Header.Get("X-TENANT-ID")
  id := req.Header.Get("X-REQUEST-ID")
  key := tenant + ":" + id
  // pseudo Redis call with TTL 120s
  ok := redis.SetNX(key, "1", 120 * time.Second)
  if !ok {
    // respond 409 with {"error":"duplicate"}
    return
  }
  // forward to backend
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test dedupe behavior under high concurrency?
- How would you scale Redis for many tenants and ensure TTL correctness?

